# ReportIQ MCP and Feed

## Programmatic access (this repo’s MCP)

When the **reportiq** MCP server is enabled and the FastAPI app is up (`REPORTIQ_API_BASE`, default `http://127.0.0.1:8000`):

- **Stakeholder overview (UI):** set the app header to **Manager** and open **`/document`** for the in-app **ReportIQ** product narrative (aligned with repo naming, not legacy “ClearPath”-only titles).
- Prefer **`reportiq_*` tools** (health, intake analyze, RAG, intake gaps, submission list/create/delete) instead of ad-hoc `curl` for the same operations.
- Intake: pass non-empty `q1_text` and optional flat `form_data` (string keys) to `reportiq_intake_analyze`, matching `POST /api/questions/intake/analyze`.
- RAG: call `reportiq_rag_construct_sentence` then `reportiq_rag_policy_quote` with the same `form_data`; pass the constructed `sentence` into `reportiq_rag_policy_quote` as `constructed_sentence` when mirroring the app.
- **Feed:** `reportiq_submission_create` appends to the same list the app uses (`GET/POST/DELETE /api/submissions`). Use `reportiq_submission_list` to read rows without a browser. The UI at `/feed` reads from that API when the backend is reachable.
- Read field keys and conditionals: fetch the **resource** `reportiq://form-schema` (see [docs/MCP.md](docs/MCP.md)).

## Browser and Feed (cursor-ide-browser or manual)

- After **Submit** on the home form (or after `reportiq_submission_create`), a new row appears on **`/feed`** when the frontend can reach the API (Vite proxies `/api` in dev).
- To verify in the browser: open the app origin, use **browser_snapshot** before structural interactions, and after any navigation. Use **browser_lock** per the host’s instructions. After `browser_navigate` to `/feed`, take a new snapshot, expand the `SubmissionRow`, and check the **Report** and **Summary** tabs for AI extraction when the intake run succeeded.
- E2E checklist: fill all sections; handle conditionals; in **AI follow-up** run the pipeline if needed, then **Submit**; navigate to **Feed** and expand the new row.

## When to use which

- **MCP (reportiq)**: health, intake, RAG, and **feed CRUD** against the shared API.
- **Browser MCP**: full wizard UI, PDF, and anything that must exercise the React app end-to-end.

## Dev note

`localhost` and `127.0.0.1` are different origins for any remaining client-only storage. The feed list itself is server-backed; use one host consistently for bookmarks and manual testing.
